    "sentence-category-reason": "Expands the algebraic square explicitly.",
    "sentence-category": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 17,
    "sentence": "Since $mn \\equiv 1 \\pmod{d}$, we have $mn = kd+1$ for some integer $k$.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "sentence-category-reason": "Infers a standard congruence representation introducing k.",
    "sentence-category": "Analyze"
  },
  {
    "index": 18,
    "sentence": "Then $n^4 - 2n^3 + 3n^2 - 2n + 1 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{mn-1}$.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "sentence-category-reason": "Applies the divisibility to state a congruence to 0 modulo mn\u22121.",
