    "sentence-category-reason": "Manipulates the inequality step-by-step to conclude a value for m.",
    "sentence-category": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 43,
    "sentence": "If $m^2-1 = (m-2)^2$, then $m^2-1 = m^2-4m+4$, so $4m=5$, which is not an integer.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "sentence-category-reason": "Assumes equality and carries out algebra to derive 4m=5 and note impossibility.",
    "sentence-category": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 44,
    "sentence": "If $m^2-1 = 0$, then $m=1$, so $n=1$.",
